      "id": "7l97bmp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Motion"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Distance measures the total path length (scalar), while displacement is the shortest straight-line path between initial and final positions (vector).",
        "Speed is the rate of change of distance, whereas velocity includes both speed and direction.",
        "Acceleration is defined as the rate of change of velocity with respect to time.",
        "The three equations of motion govern bodies undergoing uniform acceleration along a straight line.",
        "Graphical analysis of motion uses distance-time and velocity-time graphs to calculate speed, acceleration, and displacement."
      ],
      "id": "6mm1wmn"
    },
