    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Displacement can be zero even when total distance covered is non-zero (e.g., returning to the starting point).",
        "The slope of a Distance-Time graph gives Speed, while the slope of a Velocity-Time graph gives Acceleration.",
        "The area under a Velocity-Time graph represents the total Displacement covered by the object."
      ],
